                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8806e44b-a68e-3b41-855e-bdf207e3e0fd",
                        "entry_id": "0e56c811-6f51-3b00-8994-e83741eb46cd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "aftreksel van mout, gezoet en gehopt beslag voor de bereiding van bier"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "17e96a40-10a8-4548-afd1-5e64289d75de",
                        "source_entry_id": "0e56c811-6f51-3b00-8994-e83741eb46cd",
                        "source_sense_id": "8806e44b-a68e-3b41-855e-bdf207e3e0fd",
                        "source_sense_description": "aftreksel van mout",
                        "target_lang_word": "wort",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "wort",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9f4b3cb6-188e-3dbd-b04c-e9faa2e3efbe",
                                        "entry_id": "fbb17f54-e819-3b7e-b275-1d9a5df0c8a2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Now chiefly as the second element in the names of plants: a plant used for food or medicine."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ca9d4da-0d29-47ab-81ec-6660bd9ae218",
                                                "sense_id": "9f4b3cb6-188e-3dbd-b04c-e9faa2e3efbe",
                                                "text": "[T]he people of his citye, […] shulde be norysshed with barly brede and cakes of whete, and that the residue of their diete shulde be salte, olyues, chese, and likes, and more ouer wortes that the feldes do brynge furthe, for their potage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f4f54570-4b21-48cf-aa97-db517a5e29e8",
                                                "sense_id": "9f4b3cb6-188e-3dbd-b04c-e9faa2e3efbe",
                                                "text": "[H]e [a poor person] drinks vvater, and liue's of vvort leaues, pulſe, like a hog, or ſcraps like a dog, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c1de36d7-3de7-4b0e-a633-b1b230f6bdbb",
                                                "sense_id": "9f4b3cb6-188e-3dbd-b04c-e9faa2e3efbe",
                                                "text": "It is an excellent pleaſure to be able to take pleaſure in vvorts and vvater, in bread and onions; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "172b51f8-186d-42b7-8889-981848c9b6d3",
                                                "sense_id": "9f4b3cb6-188e-3dbd-b04c-e9faa2e3efbe",
                                                "text": "Two saints are credited with giving St. John's wort its name. One was St. John of Jerusalem, who used the wort (plant) during the crusades to heal his knights' battlefield wounds, and the other was John the Baptist."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "306b8e2e-8215-35f4-bcd7-3c4638439d6e",
                                        "entry_id": "fbb17f54-e819-3b7e-b275-1d9a5df0c8a2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Chiefly in the plural: a plant of the genus Brassica used as a vegetable; a brassica; especially, a cabbage (Brassica oleracea)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical",
                                            "specifically"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be903090-cb8f-46e9-9963-c77d1c5f6588",
                                                "sense_id": "306b8e2e-8215-35f4-bcd7-3c4638439d6e",
                                                "text": "VVhy (ſay they in ſcorne and contempt of povertie) here is the ſtem of a vvoort ſo vvell grovvne, here is a cabbage ſo thriven and fed, that a poore mans boord vvill not hold it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f909d65-b0c3-45cd-9020-8b837f964f88",
                                                "sense_id": "306b8e2e-8215-35f4-bcd7-3c4638439d6e",
                                                "text": "I am poore / And may expect a vvorſe; yet digging, pruning, / Mending of broken vvayes, carrying of vvater, / Planting of VVorts, and Onyons, any thing / That's honeſt, and a mans, Ile rather chooſe, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac1faad9-1e08-498b-b81a-6e3e109e770a",
                                                "sense_id": "306b8e2e-8215-35f4-bcd7-3c4638439d6e",
                                                "text": "Though ne'er ſo mean the Viands be, / They vvell content my Prevv and me. / Or Pea, or Bean, or VVort, or Beet, / VVhat ever comes, content makes ſvveet: […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9362f8ec-43a0-3ddb-9083-d75d5f3cfdf5",
                                        "entry_id": "fbb17f54-e819-3b7e-b275-1d9a5df0c8a2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A non-vascular plant growing on land from the division Anthocerotophyta (the hornworts) or Marchantiophyta (liverworts); an anthocerotophyte or marchantiophyte."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "wort",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f2c780b8-e820-3c5a-b28c-6f0c0102da71",
                                        "entry_id": "ae3ba469-6786-39ea-886e-c7aac8b523a8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Also worts: a liquid extracted from mash (ground malt or some other grain soaked in hot water), which is then fermented to make beer, or fermented and distilled to make a malt liquor such as whisky."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14bda22e-2cc7-4f5b-ace2-49148cc83a5a",
                                                "sense_id": "f2c780b8-e820-3c5a-b28c-6f0c0102da71",
                                                "text": "Nay then tvvo treyes, an if you grovv ſo nice, / Methegline, VVort, and Malmſey; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "84d54c6d-956e-4c8c-98e3-471d031016ea",
                                                "sense_id": "f2c780b8-e820-3c5a-b28c-6f0c0102da71",
                                                "text": "VVhen they make drink vvith them, they take 10 or 12 ripe Plantains and maſh them vvell in a Trough: then they put tvvo gallons of VVater among them; and this in tvvo hours time vvill ferment and froth like VVort: In four hours it is fit to drink; and then they bottle it and drink it as they have occaſion: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c752ffc0-b2c8-4360-abfa-20ef13adf9bd",
                                                "sense_id": "f2c780b8-e820-3c5a-b28c-6f0c0102da71",
                                                "text": "Making the wort with nothing but barley malt and hot water is the standard method in Germany, and in many U.S. microbreweries."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49b4e82a-57b6-45b5-b1ea-094a87b429c6",
                                                "sense_id": "f2c780b8-e820-3c5a-b28c-6f0c0102da71",
                                                "text": "They discovered what are called \"wild\" or \"spontaneously fermented\" beers, in which fermentation is induced not by pitching commercially produced yeast into an enclosed tank, but by letting the wild yeasts floating in the air interact with the wort to turn it into alcohol."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fc08aec7-0ab7-44ea-b1d2-f7e68c40df46",
                        "source_entry_id": "0e56c811-6f51-3b00-8994-e83741eb46cd",
